1
00:00:02,097 --> 00:00:04,532
Last time, in 2010,

2
00:00:04,552 --> 00:00:06,457
a crew went back to Jupiter,

3
00:00:06,477 --> 00:00:07,757
found the ship Discovery,

4
00:00:07,777 --> 00:00:10,757
and woke up its computer, HAL.

5
00:00:10,777 --> 00:00:13,557
Then Jupiter collapsed into a second sun,

6
00:00:13,577 --> 00:00:15,532
and a message reached Earth:

7
00:00:15,552 --> 00:00:18,560
all these worlds are yours, except Europa.

8
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:21,465
Dave and HAL vanished into the monolith.

9
00:00:21,485 --> 00:00:22,710
There are no more movies,

10
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:25,285
but Arthur C. Clarke wrote two more

11
00:00:25,305 --> 00:00:28,785
books, 2061 and 3001.

12
00:00:28,805 --> 00:00:31,110
Clarke called them variations on a theme,

13
00:00:31,130 --> 00:00:33,885
so some details change from book to book.

14
00:00:33,905 --> 00:00:35,435
This is part three.

15
00:00:35,455 --> 00:00:36,753
Spoilers ahead!

16
00:00:37,433 --> 00:00:40,573
It's 2061, fifty-one years later.

17
00:00:40,593 --> 00:00:42,548
Heywood Floyd is now a hundred

18
00:00:42,568 --> 00:00:44,268
and three years old.

19
00:00:44,323 --> 00:00:45,728
He lives on a space station

20
00:00:45,748 --> 00:00:47,953
in orbit, where low gravity

21
00:00:47,973 --> 00:00:50,473
has kept him healthy for decades.

22
00:00:50,558 --> 00:00:51,913
Most people his age would

23
00:00:51,933 --> 00:00:53,508
be long gone.

24
00:00:53,583 --> 00:00:54,588
But Floyd still

25
00:00:54,608 --> 00:00:56,702
has one more big trip ahead of him.

26
00:00:57,468 --> 00:00:59,123
Out in the solar system,

27
00:00:59,143 --> 00:01:01,543
Jupiter now shines as a small sun,

28
00:01:01,563 --> 00:01:03,493
and people call it Lucifer.

29
00:01:03,513 --> 00:01:05,793
Its warmth is melting Europa's ice

30
00:01:05,813 --> 00:01:07,028
into an ocean,

31
00:01:07,048 --> 00:01:10,153
and thick clouds now hide the moon from view.

32
00:01:10,173 --> 00:01:12,378
Nobody has dared to land there.

33
00:01:12,398 --> 00:01:15,503
The warning from 2010 still stands:

34
00:01:15,523 --> 00:01:17,423
Europa is off limits.

35
00:01:18,175 --> 00:01:20,480
Floyd is invited on the first voyage

36
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:21,328
of the Universe,

37
00:01:21,348 --> 00:01:25,430
a luxury spaceship with famous passengers on board.

38
00:01:25,450 --> 00:01:27,055
It's headed for Halley's Comet,

39
00:01:27,075 --> 00:01:28,630
which swings past the Sun

40
00:01:28,650 --> 00:01:31,280
about every seventy-six years.

41
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:33,305
Floyd saw it once before,

42
00:01:33,325 --> 00:01:35,280
back in 1986,

43
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:36,730
as a young man.

44
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:37,955
Now he gets to see it

45
00:01:37,975 --> 00:01:38,971
a second time.

46
00:01:39,647 --> 00:01:43,527
The Universe lands on the comet's dark, icy core.

47
00:01:43,547 --> 00:01:45,327
Floyd steps out and becomes one

48
00:01:45,347 --> 00:01:47,002
of the first people ever to walk

49
00:01:47,022 --> 00:01:48,797
on Halley's surface.

50
00:01:48,917 --> 00:01:49,997
As the comet warms

51
00:01:50,017 --> 00:01:51,397
up near the Sun,

52
00:01:51,417 --> 00:01:53,677
jets of gas and dust burst out

53
00:01:53,697 --> 00:01:55,697
of the ground like geysers.

54
00:01:55,717 --> 00:01:58,497
That's where a comet's glowing tail comes from.

55
00:01:59,192 --> 00:02:02,197
Meanwhile, Floyd's grandson Chris is an officer

56
00:02:02,217 --> 00:02:04,592
on another ship, the Galaxy.

57
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:07,162
It's exploring the moons of Jupiter,

58
00:02:07,182 --> 00:02:08,137
flying from one

59
00:02:08,157 --> 00:02:10,437
to the next to study them up close.

60
00:02:10,457 --> 00:02:12,637
It's a quiet science mission.

61
00:02:12,657 --> 00:02:14,647
Everything seems routine,

62
00:02:14,667 --> 00:02:16,322
until one of the crew turns out

63
00:02:16,342 --> 00:02:17,901
to be hiding a secret.

64
00:02:18,616 --> 00:02:21,696
A stewardess named Rose suddenly takes control

65
00:02:21,716 --> 00:02:23,216
of the Galaxy.

66
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:25,006
She forces the pilot to steer

67
00:02:25,026 --> 00:02:27,506
for Europa, the one world humans

68
00:02:27,526 --> 00:02:29,481
were warned to stay away from.

69
00:02:29,501 --> 00:02:31,131
She won't say why.

70
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:32,331
It seems someone back

71
00:02:32,351 --> 00:02:33,681
on Earth badly wants

72
00:02:33,701 --> 00:02:35,746
to know what's hidden on that moon.

73
00:02:36,422 --> 00:02:38,202
The landing goes wrong.

74
00:02:38,222 --> 00:02:40,752
The Galaxy comes down hard and splashes

75
00:02:40,772 --> 00:02:42,872
into Europa's new ocean.

76
00:02:42,947 --> 00:02:44,182
The crew survives,

77
00:02:44,202 --> 00:02:46,307
but the ship can't take off again.

78
00:02:46,327 --> 00:02:47,657
They're stranded.

79
00:02:47,677 --> 00:02:49,112
As the Galaxy floats,

80
00:02:49,132 --> 00:02:51,987
they spot something huge near the shore:

81
00:02:52,007 --> 00:02:54,630
a mountain that glitters in Lucifer's light.

82
00:02:55,230 --> 00:02:56,910
It's called Mount Zeus,

83
00:02:56,930 --> 00:02:59,285
and it's made of solid diamond.

84
00:02:59,305 --> 00:03:00,960
Deep inside Jupiter,

85
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:04,355
crushing pressure had turned carbon into diamond.

86
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:05,612
When the planet collapsed,

87
00:03:05,632 --> 00:03:07,010
a chunk of its core

88
00:03:07,030 --> 00:03:10,135
was blasted out and landed on Europa.

89
00:03:10,155 --> 00:03:11,285
A diamond the size

90
00:03:11,305 --> 00:03:12,535
of a mountain could shake

91
00:03:12,555 --> 00:03:14,635
up Earth's whole economy.

92
00:03:14,655 --> 00:03:16,135
That may be why someone wanted

93
00:03:16,155 --> 00:03:17,405
to get there first.

94
00:03:18,111 --> 00:03:19,741
The only ship that can reach them

95
00:03:19,761 --> 00:03:21,541
in time is the Universe,

96
00:03:21,561 --> 00:03:23,761
still out near Halley's Comet.

97
00:03:23,841 --> 00:03:25,946
Its captain turns around and races

98
00:03:25,966 --> 00:03:28,021
toward Jupiter at top speed,

99
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:29,971
with Floyd on board.

100
00:03:29,991 --> 00:03:31,796
Now Floyd is flying to save

101
00:03:31,816 --> 00:03:33,396
his own grandson.

102
00:03:33,416 --> 00:03:35,071
After a long chase,

103
00:03:35,091 --> 00:03:37,271
the Universe lands on Europa,

104
00:03:37,291 --> 00:03:39,232
right next to the stranded crew.

105
00:03:39,909 --> 00:03:40,614
While they wait,

106
00:03:40,634 --> 00:03:43,214
the crew glimpses Europa's new life:

107
00:03:43,234 --> 00:03:46,114
strange creatures crawling out of the sea.

108
00:03:46,134 --> 00:03:47,839
Everyone gets home safely,

109
00:03:47,859 --> 00:03:50,334
and the Europans are left in peace.

110
00:03:50,399 --> 00:03:53,104
But someone was watching all along.

111
00:03:53,124 --> 00:03:54,634
Inside the monolith,

112
00:03:54,654 --> 00:03:57,479
Dave and HAL are guarding the Europans.

113
00:03:57,579 --> 00:03:59,334
And in about a thousand years,

114
00:03:59,354 --> 00:04:00,950
humans will be judged.

115
00:04:01,691 --> 00:04:03,821
Now jump ahead a thousand years,

116
00:04:03,841 --> 00:04:06,021
to the year 3001.

117
00:04:06,041 --> 00:04:07,302
Out past Neptune,

118
00:04:07,322 --> 00:04:09,526
a space tug called Goliath

119
00:04:09,546 --> 00:04:11,476
is collecting ice comets.

120
00:04:11,496 --> 00:04:13,351
Instead, its crew finds

121
00:04:13,371 --> 00:04:15,976
a frozen body drifting in the dark.

122
00:04:15,996 --> 00:04:17,301
It's Frank Poole,

123
00:04:17,321 --> 00:04:19,226
the astronaut HAL sent spinning

124
00:04:19,246 --> 00:04:22,076
into space back in 2001.

125
00:04:22,096 --> 00:04:23,401
He's been floating out there

126
00:04:23,421 --> 00:04:25,013
for a thousand years.

127
00:04:25,779 --> 00:04:27,859
Doctors of the future bring Frank back

128
00:04:27,879 --> 00:04:29,634
to life, which takes months

129
00:04:29,654 --> 00:04:31,184
of careful work.

130
00:04:31,204 --> 00:04:32,834
When he finally wakes up,

131
00:04:32,854 --> 00:04:34,684
he's the only person alive

132
00:04:34,704 --> 00:04:36,859
from the year 2001.

133
00:04:36,879 --> 00:04:40,284
His guide is a historian named Indra Wallace.

134
00:04:40,304 --> 00:04:41,284
She helps him catch

135
00:04:41,304 --> 00:04:42,584
up on a thousand years

136
00:04:42,604 --> 00:04:44,366
of history he slept through.

137
00:04:45,152 --> 00:04:47,082
Earth looks different now.

138
00:04:47,102 --> 00:04:48,882
Four giant towers rise

139
00:04:48,902 --> 00:04:50,432
from the equator all the way

140
00:04:50,452 --> 00:04:51,932
up into space.

141
00:04:51,952 --> 00:04:52,932
At the top,

142
00:04:52,952 --> 00:04:54,132
they hold up a ring

143
00:04:54,152 --> 00:04:55,389
around the whole planet,

144
00:04:55,409 --> 00:04:59,132
a city in orbit where people live and work.

145
00:04:59,152 --> 00:05:01,862
Elevators run up and down the towers,

146
00:05:01,882 --> 00:05:03,537
so nobody needs a rocket

147
00:05:03,557 --> 00:05:04,805
to reach space.

148
00:05:05,515 --> 00:05:07,405
Instead of phones or screens,

149
00:05:07,425 --> 00:05:08,965
people wear BrainCaps,

150
00:05:08,985 --> 00:05:12,060
which connect their minds straight to computers.

151
00:05:12,195 --> 00:05:13,085
To wear one,

152
00:05:13,105 --> 00:05:15,035
you have to shave your head.

153
00:05:15,055 --> 00:05:16,385
Frank tries one,

154
00:05:16,405 --> 00:05:19,485
and information pours straight into his brain.

155
00:05:19,505 --> 00:05:21,260
It's like the internet he knew,

156
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:23,699
except the screen is inside his head.

157
00:05:24,452 --> 00:05:25,907
Frank wants to see the place

158
00:05:25,927 --> 00:05:28,002
where his old mission ended.

159
00:05:28,087 --> 00:05:29,842
So he joins Captain Chandler

160
00:05:29,862 --> 00:05:31,417
of the Goliath on a trip out

161
00:05:31,437 --> 00:05:33,267
to Jupiter's moons.

162
00:05:33,287 --> 00:05:35,417
Humans now live on Ganymede,

163
00:05:35,437 --> 00:05:37,417
under the light of Lucifer.

164
00:05:37,437 --> 00:05:40,492
From there, Frank looks across at Europa,

165
00:05:40,512 --> 00:05:42,840
the one world that's still off limits.

166
00:05:43,582 --> 00:05:45,557
Frank flies down to Europa,

167
00:05:45,577 --> 00:05:47,582
and something reaches out to him.

168
00:05:47,602 --> 00:05:48,817
It's Dave Bowman,

169
00:05:48,837 --> 00:05:50,342
or a copy of him,

170
00:05:50,362 --> 00:05:52,542
living inside the monolith.

171
00:05:52,562 --> 00:05:54,067
Dave and HAL have merged

172
00:05:54,087 --> 00:05:56,557
into one mind, called Halman.

173
00:05:56,577 --> 00:05:57,832
For a thousand years,

174
00:05:57,852 --> 00:06:00,257
Halman has been inside the machine,

175
00:06:00,277 --> 00:06:02,407
quietly learning how it works.

176
00:06:03,172 --> 00:06:05,177
Halman explains the truth.

177
00:06:05,197 --> 00:06:07,352
The monolith is not a god.

178
00:06:07,372 --> 00:06:08,327
It's a machine,

179
00:06:08,347 --> 00:06:12,227
built by unknown makers far out among the stars.

180
00:06:12,247 --> 00:06:14,127
Back in 2001,

181
00:06:14,147 --> 00:06:15,877
when humans dug up the monolith

182
00:06:15,897 --> 00:06:16,877
on the Moon,

183
00:06:16,897 --> 00:06:18,952
it sent a report about us.

184
00:06:18,972 --> 00:06:21,637
That message took centuries to arrive,

185
00:06:21,657 --> 00:06:23,162
and the answer took centuries

186
00:06:23,182 --> 00:06:24,191
to come back.

187
00:06:24,881 --> 00:06:26,636
Now the answer has arrived,

188
00:06:26,656 --> 00:06:28,361
and it's bad news.

189
00:06:28,381 --> 00:06:30,111
The makers have judged humans

190
00:06:30,131 --> 00:06:31,546
to be dangerous,

191
00:06:31,566 --> 00:06:33,271
and the monolith's new orders

192
00:06:33,291 --> 00:06:35,541
are to wipe out humanity.

193
00:06:35,596 --> 00:06:37,501
The same machine that taught apes

194
00:06:37,521 --> 00:06:41,076
to use tools now plans to end the story.

195
00:06:41,096 --> 00:06:42,751
Humans have very little time

196
00:06:42,771 --> 00:06:43,854
to fight back.

197
00:06:44,505 --> 00:06:46,585
But humans have dangerous tools

198
00:06:46,605 --> 00:06:47,885
of their own.

199
00:06:47,905 --> 00:06:49,385
Deep inside a mountain

200
00:06:49,405 --> 00:06:51,260
on the Moon called Pico,

201
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:53,085
there's a sealed vault.

202
00:06:53,105 --> 00:06:55,860
It holds the most dangerous computer viruses

203
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:57,830
ever made, locked away

204
00:06:57,850 --> 00:06:59,850
so they can never escape.

205
00:06:59,875 --> 00:07:02,782
Frank's team carefully takes out the worst of them.

206
00:07:03,494 --> 00:07:06,599
Halman carries the viruses into the monolith,

207
00:07:06,619 --> 00:07:08,174
hidden inside himself,

208
00:07:08,194 --> 00:07:09,474
like the Trojan horse

209
00:07:09,494 --> 00:07:11,324
in the old Greek story.

210
00:07:11,344 --> 00:07:12,899
The plan works.

211
00:07:12,919 --> 00:07:15,074
The virus spreads from one monolith

212
00:07:15,094 --> 00:07:16,099
to the next,

213
00:07:16,119 --> 00:07:17,574
and they shut down for good,

214
00:07:17,594 --> 00:07:19,274
before they can strike.

215
00:07:19,294 --> 00:07:20,729
Humanity is safe,

216
00:07:20,749 --> 00:07:21,909
at least for now.

217
00:07:22,617 --> 00:07:24,052
So that's the whole odyssey,

218
00:07:24,072 --> 00:07:27,012
across four books and a thousand years.

219
00:07:27,032 --> 00:07:29,782
A monolith taught apes to use tools.

220
00:07:29,887 --> 00:07:31,776
Another called humans to Jupiter.

221
00:07:31,796 --> 00:07:35,057
A third turned Jupiter into a sun.

222
00:07:35,157 --> 00:07:36,087
And in the end,

223
00:07:36,107 --> 00:07:37,787
humans used their own tools

224
00:07:37,807 --> 00:07:39,087
to stop them.

225
00:07:39,107 --> 00:07:40,462
Clarke ends with a hint

226
00:07:40,482 --> 00:07:42,837
that the makers may notice someday.

227
00:07:42,857 --> 00:07:45,423
Until then, the future belongs to us.

